{"id": "EUVD-2026-76849", "enisaUuid": "bf8b7f1d-1308-3438-8273-f1b40b9f3918", "description": "msgpack-java through 0.9.12 contains an integer overflow vulnerability in MessageUnpacker.skipValue() when processing MAP32 containers with large element counts. Attackers can supply a MAP32 element count at or above 0x40000000 that wraps when doubled, causing the parser cursor to desynchronize and attacker-controlled data to be returned in place of later fields.", "datePublished": "2026-09-12T11:06:12", "dateUpdated": "2026-09-24T14:21:44", "baseScore": 6.9, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:L/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/msgpack/msgpack-java/issues/1014", "https://github.com/msgpack/msgpack-java/blob/v0.9.12/msgpack-core/src/main/java/org/msgpack/core/MessageUnpacker.java#L573-L581", "https://github.com/msgpack/msgpack-java", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/msgpack-java-through-0.9.12-integer-overflow-via-map32"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-90473", "GHSA-9vjp-f3jg-99pq"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.41, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "e4021275-781c-3ca2-9a89-aa8e9ae6dbe0", "product": {"name": "msgpack-java", "vendor": {"name": "msgpack"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22640.9.12"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "2c215f3f-bc86-34d5-a83e-3fe51a5177bb", "vendor": {"name": "msgpack"}}], "isExploited": false}